# - internal/actions/ctl.go, internal/corazawaf/transaction.go and waf.go:
#   ctl:ruleRemoveTargetById, ByTag and ByMsg, and ctl:ruleRemoveByTag and
#   ByMsg, walked every rule by value on every request, and a target
#   removal then added an entry per selected rule, one allocation each.
#   ctl:ruleRemoveTargetByTag=OWASP_CRS selects every CRS rule, which cost
#   68 us and 720 allocations a request. A ctl caches the IDs it selects
#   per rule group, and the removals share one capped slice: 24 us and 118
#   allocations.
#   Upstream: issue #1848 and PR #1849 (2026-11-08), open at 08aa511.
